From 1e53c4b20f4876273fecdea37e6eb7b2a885c6c6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: greyoak111 <151205158+greyoak111@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 00:29:12 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 14/30] Renew the Bilibili login and end it on the server at
 sign-out

SessionMaintenance follows the web flow: cookie/info, RSA-OAEP(SHA-256)
of refresh_<ms> under the public key shipped in the main site's
wasm_rsa_encrypt_bg.wasm (modulus copied from it), correspond/1 for
refresh_csrf, cookie/refresh, then confirm/refresh. The coordinator
checks when the account becomes ready and every 12 hours, never while
the room is live, one run at a time; the renewed login is saved before
the old token is retired and any failure keeps the current login.
Sign-out also calls login/exit/v2 (as the web header does). Outcomes are
logged by step name only.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
